  "observations": [
    "Both runs accepted with identical physical score and geometry; all final non-GDS artifact hashes match and GDS differs only by timestamp fields.",
    "Magic DRC is single-threaded: both runs average ~100% CPU, one thread, user CPU approximately equals wall time, reported I/O wait zero. Its cloud user CPU time is longer by ~31%.",
    "Detailed routing averages ~3.8 CPUs on both hosts and reports zero I/O wait; cloud user CPU time and wall time are both ~20% larger. Eight observed OS threads are not eight continuously busy cores.",
    "Official precheck invokes deep:true tiled:false threads:4 on both hosts. Later logged 14/8 thread capability refers to tiled mode, which is disabled.",
    "Official DRC connectivity setup grows from 36m20s to 45m29s, accounting for 549s of 571s added DRC runtime.",
    "Final GDS LVS is ~17s faster on cloud, so hardware difference is workload-specific.",
    "The total comparison is a single run on each host; seeds differ for digital tests, and historical host-load conditions were not controlled."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    "The dominant physical slowdown is CPU execution throughput for the same workload, not different physical designs or reported storage wait. CPU microarchitecture, clock speed, scheduling/SMT, and translation behavior require host data or matched probes to separate.",
    "Extra memory and advertised vCPU count do not automatically accelerate the single-threaded dominant checks.",
    "File-mtime proxy from last compiled candidate.vvp write to last simulation.log write is 233.742s versus 437.464s; ~204s additional gate-simulation interval, including small process/container transitions. Do not claim exact vvp CPU time without instrumentation."
  ],
